   "url": "https://www.nps.gov/gate/learn/historyculture/great-kills-park.htm",
   "status": 200,
   "final_url": "https://www.nps.gov/gate/learn/historyculture/great-kills-park.htm",
   "title": "Great Kills Park - Gateway National Recreation Area (U.S. National Park Service)",
   "text": "An official website of the United States government\nSearch or ask anything\nAsk DOI Anything - How Can We Help?\nHelp me plan a visit to Gateway National Recreation Area\nWhere can I swim, boat, or fish at Gateway National Recreation Area?\nAre there ranger programs or events at Gateway National Recreation Area?\nAre there alerts or closures at Gateway National Recreation Area?\nSkip to global NPS navigation\nSkip to this park navigation\nSkip to the main content\nSkip to this park information section\nSkip to the footer section\nNational Park Service\nOpen\nMenu\nGateway National Recreation Area\nPlan Your Visit\nLearn About the Park\nGet Involved\nInfo\nAlerts 6\nMaps\nCalendar\nFees\nGreat Kills Park\nON THIS PAGE\nNAVIGATION\nGreat Kills Park\nNPS Photo/Jason Wickersty\nGreat Kills Park is a 523 acre park located on the south shore of Staten Island. This site was created by Robert Moses and operated by New York City Department of Parks and Recreation between 1947 and 1972. Great Kills Park became part of the National Park Service in 1972 when Gateway National Recreation Area was established. Great Kills Park has several public recreation facilities including a beach center, a life-guarded beach, a multi-use path, hiking and biking trails, fishing areas, a marina and a boat launch. We offer ranger-led programs throughout the year. Visit our event calendar to see what's happening this week.\nParking to fish at Crooke's Point requires a permit. 2026 permits will be sold from March 2, 2026, through March 31 on recreation.gov.\nIf you want to know more about the Great Kills Park Environmental Cleanup Project please visit here.\nOperating Hours\nGreat Kills is open daily from from 6 am to 9 pm, except by permit.\nFacilities\nGreat Kills Marina: Moonbeam Great Kills Marina serves boaters at Great Kills Harbor. Call (718) 351-8476 for more information.\nMulti Use Path: Walk, run or bicycle along this path. About 1.5 miles either way.\nSwimming Beach: Open from Memorial Day weekend through Labor Day. Lifeguards are on duty from 10 am - 6 pm daily.\nBoat Ramp: A permit is required for parking in this area. 2026 permits will be sold from March 2 through March 31 on recreation.gov.\nPlease Remember:\nA Boat Launch Permit is required to park within the Boat Launch Parking Area .\nA boat trailer must be attached to your vehicle within the Boat Launch Parking Area.\nBoat Launch Parking is limited to 24 hours per visit.\nCommercial activity is prohibited.\nPersonal watercraft, such as jet-skis, kayaks, canoes or any other personal watercraft are prohibited at the Great Kills Park Boat Launch.\nDriving Directions\nVerrrazano Narrows Bridge from Brooklyn or the Goethals or Bayonne Bridges from New Jersey to the Staten Island Expressway (Interstate 278).\nTake the Hylan Boulevard exit.\nProceed south on Hylan Boulevard.\nTurn left at the entrance to Great Kills Park.\nPublic Transportation\nTake the S78 from the Staten Island Ferry Terminal or the S79 from 95th St & 4th Avenue (Brooklyn) to the park entrance on Hylan Blvd.\nLast updated: February 25, 2026\nWas this page helpful?\nYes\nNo\nAn official form of the United States government. Provided by Touchpoints\nPark footer\nCONTACT INFO\nMailing Address:\n210 New York Avenue\nStaten Island, NY 10305\nPhone:\n718 354-4606\nContact Us\nTOOLS\nSite Index\nEspañol\nSTAY CONNECTED\nExperience Your America.\nDownload the NPS app to navigate the parks on the go.\nSearch\nAccessibility\nPrivacy Policy\nFOIA\nNotices\nContact Gateway National Recreation Area\nNPS FAQ\nNo Fear Act\nDisclaimer\nVulnerability Disclosure Policy\nUSA.gov\nOffice of Civil Rights\nLooking for U.S. government information and services? Visit USA.gov",
